# D3: exactness of the quad. The gate's matrix plan on c2-packed-tp4-gate-quad (quad ON, every audit on, QWEN_FAST_DRAFT_SINGLES_AUDIT=all):
# four real-text users at 2,560 / 3,072 / 4,096 / 16,384 tokens - ALL past the 2,048-row draft window, so the concurrent arm's
# packed-4 rounds are quad rounds - 256 tokens out, a concurrent arm (the quad drafts) and a solo arm (the same prompts one at a time:
# a lone user never batches, so this is the singles reference on the same image), strict policy: every concurrent text must equal its
# solo text. Users 2 and 3 are the speed window's E1 prompts (the real-text corpus fixes a prompt by user index and length; E1 ran
# 512 / 1,536 / 4,096 / 16,384 at 256 tokens out), so their texts and solo accepted-prefix sequences are compared with E1's.
# The text is the target's own whatever is drafted; the DRAFTS are judged three ways: the in-model singles audit (every quad round, bit
# for bit, in the container log), the concurrent arm's per-request accepted-prefix sequences against the solo arm's by position
# (speed_window_compare.py --batched-vs-singles), and the solo sequences against E1's.
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the four-card batched-draft window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it):
# copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/draft and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here
# names a rig, a card or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG names the image D0 builds from this same commit; a later commit needs a new tag.
# C2_GATE_JIT=record: the growth of the kernel cache is recorded, not judged (no four-card warm plan exists).
# Duration (estimate): reset 1-3 min; per arm an engine build 5-15 min plus 4-10 min of streams (the audit replays every user each
# round): 25 / 45 / 120 min.
# Read: the gate verdict per arm; per user IDENTICAL concurrent against solo; the audits clean (extent, T1, T2); zero refusals; the
# [ACCEPT] line (tokens per round in the concurrent arm); in the concurrent arm's server log the quad marker once, the '[QUAD-DRAFT]
# round=' lines and every '[DRAFT-SINGLES-AUDIT]' line equal=1 (their count is the audited quad rounds: at least 20 are wanted, a
# handful proves nothing); the divergence records file if any user differs. Then, offline:
#   python scripts/ci/speed_window_compare.py <D3 results> --batched-vs-singles
#   python scripts/ci/speed_window_compare.py <E1 results> <D3 results> --users 2,3
# STOP on FAIL, NOT_COMPARABLE, UNSTABLE, an audit mismatch, an unequal [DRAFT-SINGLES-AUDIT] line, and on any difference from the
# singles or from E1 in the compares (offline, exit 1; exit 2 is too few shared positions: re-run with longer answers).
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset gate
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-draft-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-gate-quad
C2_GATE_PLAN=matrix
C2_GATE_LENGTHS=2560,3072,4096,16384
C2_GATE_MAX_TOKENS=256
C2_GATE_JIT=record
